            0.086,
            0.882,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "**Q.3. The first number has prime factorisation 2 × 3 × 7 and the second number has prime factorisation 3 × 7 × 11. Are they co-prime? Does one of them divide the other?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.131,
            0.397,
            0.148
          ],
          "content": "Ans. No, they are not co-prime."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.158,
            0.518,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": "No, one of them is not dividing the other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.185,
            0.718,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "**Q.4. Guna says, “Any two prime numbers are co-prime”. Is he right?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.212,
            0.58,
            0.23
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Yes, for example 2, 3; 3,11 (Try other examples)"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.266,
            0.218,
            0.283
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Section 5.5"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.294,
            0.233,
            0.311
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page no. 124"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
